	(text "DRIVE IO (record sections 11-12; SPEC rulings: 3.3 V RS485 non-isolated, quadrature via 74AHCT125, JST GH signals). Connectors are generic placeholders: operator picks parts and pin order.\nU9 THVD1450 from a P4 UART in RS485 half-duplex mode; DE and /RE tied, one GPIO. R23 termination fitted-not-populated (short point-to-point run).\nU10: 3.3 V GPIO in (TTL thresholds), 5 V out to the drive's opto inputs. PU- and DIR- to GND, single-ended as on the bench board. Channels 3-4 spare (OE high, inputs grounded).\nJ4 comms: 485_5V (drive pin 10) is ours to supply; COM (drive pin 6) is the reference for the 485 section AND the opto outputs. Keep GND between supply and signals.\nStatus: WR alarm (pin 7), RDY/PF following error (pin 8), ZO encoder index (pin 9): opto NPN pulling to COM, so pull-ups here plus series R.\nTODO(detailing): ESD on every pin that leaves the board, pin order on J4/J5, 3.3 V vs 5 V pull-up for the opto outputs."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
